      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When facing community opposition to a high-density multi-family residential project, common arguments tend to revolve around concerns about property values, lifestyle, traffic, parking, and character of the neighborhood. Citizens may worry that increased density will lead to decreased property values, increased noise and traffic congestion, or alter the neighborhood's aesthetic and cohesion. They may also express concerns about the impact on local schools, community parks, or the overall quality of life in the area.",
